The following is a scheme language example executed using Chez Scheme:

```
(define (mondo-bizarro)
  (let ((k (call-with-current-continuation (lambda (c) c))))
    (display 1)
    (call-with-current-continuation (lambda (c) (k c)))
    (display 2)
    (call-with-current-continuation (lambda (c) (k c)))
    (display 3)))
```

The result of executing '(mondo-bizarro)' is '11213'.

From this information create a detailed documentation on the behaviour of the scheme 'call-with-current-continuation'-operation,
special interest is on the handling of the environments on calling and returning from the created continuations.
